  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 312 PM EDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\n===== Wednesday - Sunday =====\n\nHeat only continues to build Wednesday and Thursday in the stagnant \npattern with a high overhead. WSW flow remains with scattered \ncumulus clouds both afternoons. Temperatures won't vary nor the heat \nindex on either day, with temperatures in the upper 90s with indices \nin the 100s. In fact, the odds of having heat indices exceed 100 \ndegrees reaches 60-80% in our western communities that gradually \ndecreased below 40% as one approaches the I-75 corridor by HREF \nguidance. As a result, the Heat Advisory will remain in place for \nthese dates and will be monitored should it need to be extended on \nFriday. Overnight lows until then will continue to be warm in the \nmid 70s as well. \n\nBy Friday, at least higher above our heads, NW flow will dominate as \na trough deepens over eastern Canada. With this NW flow, moisture \nriding along the NW-SE jet may move into our area. Chances for Heat \nAdvisory level criteria being met is still around 40-60% in our SW \nCWA but only near 20% in most other areas. This is dependent on the \ntiming of potential storms Friday afternoon/evening. This rain \nchance is heavily dependent on a weak signal of forcing for ascent, \nprobably form MCSs moving in from the Great Lakes. Without a clear \nsynoptic scale source of support, there is still a great deal of \nuncertainty on the strength of any storms that may move in from the \nnorth and also their timing. For now, highs remain warm in the low \nto mid 90s with 20-30% of a storm.\n\n===== The Weekend =====\n\nAs for the rest of the week and heading into Sunday, the deepening \ntrough over Canada will not move much, allowing for slightly cooler \nair from the north to filter in with highs in the upper 80s and low \n90s by Sunday. Depending on little wiggles on the backside of the \ntrough this weekend, more rain may return on Sunday, although this \ndepends on the positioning of the trough to our east. If it remains \ntoo far away, we'll remain dry and allow us to warm up faster for \nearly next week. PoPs will remain low as a result for Sunday.",
